1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:29,980
Thank you.

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:39,920
Krishnamurti, in dialogue with Dr. Alan W. Anderson.

3
00:00:41,280 --> 00:00:43,120
J. Krishnamurti was born in

4
00:00:43,120 --> 00:00:44,960
South India and educated in England.

5
00:00:45,760 --> 00:00:49,350
For the past 40 years, he has been speaking in the

6
00:00:49,350 --> 00:00:52,940
United States, Europe, India, Australia, and other parts of the world.

7
00:00:53,360 --> 00:00:56,490
From the outset of his life's work, he

8
00:00:56,490 --> 00:00:59,620
repudiated all connections with organized religions and ideologies,

9
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:02,800
and said that his only concern

10
00:01:02,800 --> 00:01:05,600
was to set men absolutely unconditionally free.

11
00:01:06,540 --> 00:01:11,590
He is the author of many books, among them The Awakening of Intelligence,

12
00:01:11,590 --> 00:01:16,640
The Urgency of Change, Freedom from the Known, and The Flight of the Eagle.

13
00:01:17,660 --> 00:01:20,250
This is one of a series of

14
00:01:20,250 --> 00:01:22,840
dialogues between Krishnamurti and Dr. Alan W. Anderson,

15
00:01:23,220 --> 00:01:24,980
who is professor of religious

16
00:01:24,980 --> 00:01:26,740
studies at San Diego State University,

17
00:01:26,940 --> 00:01:29,260
where he teaches Indian and Chinese scriptures,

18
00:01:29,260 --> 00:01:31,000
and the oracular tradition.

19
00:01:32,100 --> 00:01:35,580
Dr. Anderson, a published poet, received his degree

20
00:01:35,580 --> 00:01:39,060
from Columbia University and the Union Theological Seminary.

21
00:01:39,680 --> 00:01:42,270
He has been honored with a Distinguished

22
00:01:42,270 --> 00:01:44,860
Teaching Award from the California State Universities.

23
00:01:46,520 --> 00:01:50,400
Mr. Krishnamurti, in this series of conversations,

24
00:01:50,400 --> 00:01:52,210
we've been exploring the general

25
00:01:52,210 --> 00:01:54,020
question of the transformation of man,

26
00:01:54,200 --> 00:01:56,390
a transformation which, as you

27
00:01:56,390 --> 00:01:58,580
say, is not dependent on knowledge,

28
00:01:59,260 --> 00:02:01,260
but on the ability to understand the world.

29
00:02:01,260 --> 00:02:03,620
And as I recall, we arrived

30
00:02:03,620 --> 00:02:05,980
at a point that was very crucial,

31
00:02:05,980 --> 00:02:08,360
namely the one concerned

32
00:02:08,360 --> 00:02:10,740
with relationship and communication.

33
00:02:10,740 --> 00:02:14,800
I remember one point in our conversation

34
00:02:14,800 --> 00:02:18,860
together that was extremely instructive for me,

35
00:02:18,860 --> 00:02:21,440
a point at which, when you asked

36
00:02:21,440 --> 00:02:24,020
me a question, I began to answer it,

37
00:02:24,020 --> 00:02:29,140
and you interrupted me, and reminded the viewers and me,

38
00:02:29,140 --> 00:02:29,190
Dr. Anderson, a published poet, who was a

39
00:02:29,190 --> 00:02:29,240
professor of religious studies at San Diego State University,

40
00:02:29,240 --> 00:02:32,840
that the important thing here is

41
00:02:32,840 --> 00:02:36,440
not to finish out of theoretical construction,

42
00:02:36,440 --> 00:02:41,000
rather to attain to the right beginning point,

43
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:42,930
so that we don't go

44
00:02:42,930 --> 00:02:44,860
beyond where we haven't yet begun.

45
00:02:45,920 --> 00:02:49,400
This, as I repeat, was extremely instructive for me,

46
00:02:49,640 --> 00:02:53,320
and I was thinking, if it's agreeable with you,

47
00:02:53,360 --> 00:02:56,240
that it would be helpful today if we could

48
00:02:56,240 --> 00:02:59,120
begin at the point of a concern for communication.

49
00:02:59,120 --> 00:03:01,120
And relationship.

50
00:03:01,120 --> 00:03:04,680
To go into that question, begin to unravel it.

51
00:03:04,680 --> 00:03:06,680
Unravel it, quite.

52
00:03:09,400 --> 00:03:15,800
I wonder, sir, what that word communication means.

53
00:03:17,200 --> 00:03:25,320
To communicate implies not only verbally,

54
00:03:25,800 --> 00:03:27,800
but also

55
00:03:27,800 --> 00:03:29,000
the

56
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:30,240
listening,

57
00:03:32,360 --> 00:03:34,760
in which there is a sharing,

58
00:03:36,120 --> 00:03:38,440
a thinking together,

59
00:03:38,440 --> 00:03:42,400
not accepting something that you or I say,

60
00:03:42,400 --> 00:03:48,440
but sharing together, thinking together, creating together,

61
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:54,040
all that is involved in that word communicate.

62
00:03:55,680 --> 00:03:56,680
And

63
00:03:58,400 --> 00:03:58,880
in that word,

64
00:03:58,880 --> 00:04:03,920
in that word is implied also the art of listening.

65
00:04:05,920 --> 00:04:07,920
The art of listening

66
00:04:09,480 --> 00:04:15,560
demands a quality of attention

67
00:04:15,960 --> 00:04:21,800
in which there is real listening,

68
00:04:22,360 --> 00:04:27,880
real sense of having an insight

69
00:04:27,880 --> 00:04:29,880
as we go along.

70
00:04:31,040 --> 00:04:31,600
Yes.

71
00:04:31,600 --> 00:04:32,280
It's second,

72
00:04:32,280 --> 00:04:35,920
not at the end, but at the beginning.

73
00:04:36,480 --> 00:04:37,960
So that we are

74
00:04:38,280 --> 00:04:41,280
together, walking together all the time.

75
00:04:41,280 --> 00:04:41,920
Yes, yes.

76
00:04:41,920 --> 00:04:42,400
Right.

77
00:04:42,400 --> 00:04:45,760
There's a concurrent activity here.

78
00:04:46,080 --> 00:04:49,960
Not one making a statement, the other thinking about it,

79
00:04:49,960 --> 00:04:53,440
and then saying, well, I agree, I don't agree,

80
00:04:53,440 --> 00:04:55,120
I accept, I don't accept, these

81
00:04:55,120 --> 00:04:56,800
are the reasons I don't accept,

82
00:04:56,800 --> 00:04:57,800
these are the reasons I do.

83
00:04:57,800 --> 00:04:59,920
But we are walking together.

84
00:04:59,920 --> 00:05:01,480
Walking, journeying together,

85
00:05:01,480 --> 00:05:03,440
walking together on the same path.

86
00:05:03,440 --> 00:05:04,320
Side by side.

87
00:05:04,320 --> 00:05:04,760
Yes.

88
00:05:04,760 --> 00:05:08,280
On the same road, with the same attention,

89
00:05:08,280 --> 00:05:11,200
with the same intensity, at the same time.

90
00:05:11,200 --> 00:05:12,920
Otherwise there is no communication.

91
00:05:12,920 --> 00:05:15,280
Exactly. Exactly.

92
00:05:15,280 --> 00:05:18,320
Communication implies there must be

93
00:05:20,480 --> 00:05:24,040
at the same level, at the same time,

94
00:05:24,040 --> 00:05:27,200
with the same intensity, we are walking together.

95
00:05:27,200 --> 00:05:31,280
We are thinking together, we are observing together,

96
00:05:31,280 --> 00:05:33,080
sharing together.

97
00:05:33,080 --> 00:05:37,680
Would you say that this requires an activity

98
00:05:37,680 --> 00:05:41,680
that underlies the speaking together,

99
00:05:41,680 --> 00:05:45,680
or does one come to the activity

100
00:05:45,680 --> 00:05:48,680
after one has started to speak together?

101
00:05:48,680 --> 00:05:52,040
No, sir, we are not saying

102
00:05:52,040 --> 00:05:55,400
what is the art of listening.

103
00:05:55,400 --> 00:05:56,280
Aren't we?

104
00:05:56,280 --> 00:05:56,840
Yes.

105
00:05:56,840 --> 00:06:00,960
The art of listening implies, doesn't it,

106
00:06:00,960 --> 00:06:05,440
that there is not only the verbal understanding

107
00:06:05,440 --> 00:06:07,239
between you and me,

108
00:06:07,239 --> 00:06:10,239
because we are both speaking English,

109
00:06:10,239 --> 00:06:12,519
and we know the meaning

110
00:06:12,519 --> 00:06:14,799
of each word, more or less,

111
00:06:14,799 --> 00:06:18,839
and at the same time

112
00:06:18,839 --> 00:06:22,880
we are sharing the problem together,

113
00:06:22,880 --> 00:06:25,919
sharing the issue together.

114
00:06:25,920 --> 00:06:27,680
Because, as you said, it is

115
00:06:27,680 --> 00:06:29,440
a matter of life and death.

116
00:06:29,440 --> 00:06:30,440
Absolutely.

117
00:06:30,440 --> 00:06:33,740
If you and I are both

118
00:06:33,740 --> 00:06:37,040
serious, we are sharing the thing.

119
00:06:37,040 --> 00:06:44,040
So, in communication,

120
00:06:44,040 --> 00:06:48,040
there is not only a verbal communication,

121
00:06:48,040 --> 00:06:54,040
but there is a non-verbal communication,

122
00:06:54,040 --> 00:06:54,960
which is really what is

123
00:06:54,960 --> 00:06:55,880
the meaning of life and death.

124
00:06:55,880 --> 00:06:58,960
Which comes into being,

125
00:06:58,960 --> 00:07:01,760
or which happens when one has the art

126
00:07:01,760 --> 00:07:04,960
of really listening to somebody,

127
00:07:04,960 --> 00:07:08,159
in which there is no acceptance, no denial,

128
00:07:08,159 --> 00:07:11,080
or comparison, or judgement,

129
00:07:11,080 --> 00:07:14,800
just the act of listening.

130
00:07:14,800 --> 00:07:18,440
I wonder whether I am on the right track here,

131
00:07:18,440 --> 00:07:25,440
if I suggest that there is a relation

132
00:07:25,440 --> 00:07:27,680
that is very deep here between communication

133
00:07:27,680 --> 00:07:30,680
and what we call in English, communion.

134
00:07:30,680 --> 00:07:32,280
Communion, yes.

135
00:07:32,280 --> 00:07:36,120
So that if we are in communion,

136
00:07:36,120 --> 00:07:38,320
our chance of communicating...

137
00:07:38,320 --> 00:07:41,120
Becomes simpler. Right.

138
00:07:41,120 --> 00:07:45,040
Now, to be in communion with each other,

139
00:07:45,040 --> 00:07:47,920
we must have...

140
00:07:47,920 --> 00:07:54,040
both of us must be serious about the same problem.

141
00:07:54,040 --> 00:07:55,200
At the same time,

142
00:07:55,200 --> 00:07:57,200
we must have the same passion,

143
00:07:57,200 --> 00:07:59,440
otherwise there is no communication.

144
00:07:59,440 --> 00:08:01,159
Exactly.

145
00:08:01,159 --> 00:08:03,880
If you are not interested in what is being said,

146
00:08:03,880 --> 00:08:05,440
well, you will think of something else

147
00:08:05,440 --> 00:08:09,640
and communication stops.

148
00:08:09,640 --> 00:08:13,039
So, there is a verbal communication

149
00:08:13,039 --> 00:08:15,880
and a non-verbal communication.

150
00:08:15,880 --> 00:08:20,080
They are both operating at the same time.

151
00:08:20,080 --> 00:08:22,840
One doesn't precede the other,

152
00:08:22,840 --> 00:08:24,520
or follow upon the other.

153
00:08:24,520 --> 00:08:25,159
It is...

154
00:08:25,160 --> 00:08:28,480
Yes. They move together.

155
00:08:28,480 --> 00:08:34,440
Which means that each of us, being serious,

156
00:08:34,440 --> 00:08:41,679
give our attention completely to the issue.

157
00:08:41,679 --> 00:08:47,920
That act of seriousness that takes place

158
00:08:47,920 --> 00:08:52,480
then requires the utmost devoted attention.

159
00:08:52,480 --> 00:08:54,480
Sir, but... Yes.

160
00:08:54,480 --> 00:08:59,760
A man who is really serious lives.

161
00:08:59,760 --> 00:09:01,480
Not the man who is flippant

162
00:09:01,480 --> 00:09:03,560
or merely wanting to be entertained.

163
00:09:03,560 --> 00:09:07,480
He doesn't live.

164
00:09:07,480 --> 00:09:12,200
The general notion of being serious about something

165
00:09:12,200 --> 00:09:17,760
generally suggests either undergoing some pain

166
00:09:17,760 --> 00:09:19,720
about something,

167
00:09:19,720 --> 00:09:21,960
or I am serious about something

168
00:09:21,960 --> 00:09:23,800
in order to get something else.

169
00:09:23,800 --> 00:09:29,560
These two things, as a rule,

170
00:09:29,560 --> 00:09:33,040
are what persons imagine by seriousness.

171
00:09:33,040 --> 00:09:36,719
As a matter of fact, we often hear this expression,

172
00:09:36,719 --> 00:09:38,040
don't look so serious.

173
00:09:38,040 --> 00:09:39,400
Yes. Don't we?

174
00:09:39,400 --> 00:09:40,520
Yes.

175
00:09:40,520 --> 00:09:44,280
It is as though we fear something about the serious.

176
00:09:44,280 --> 00:09:50,439
Sir, look, as we said yesterday,

177
00:09:50,439 --> 00:09:52,800
the world is in a mess.

178
00:09:52,800 --> 00:09:53,680
Yes.

179
00:09:53,680 --> 00:09:57,120
And it is my responsibility, living in this world,

180
00:09:57,120 --> 00:10:00,640
as a human being who has created this mess,

181
00:10:00,640 --> 00:10:04,359
it is my responsibility to be serious

182
00:10:04,359 --> 00:10:08,400
in the resolution of this problem.

183
00:10:08,400 --> 00:10:10,800
I am serious. It doesn't mean I am long-faced,

184
00:10:10,800 --> 00:10:12,660
I am miserable, unhappy, or

185
00:10:12,660 --> 00:10:14,520
I want something out of it.

186
00:10:14,520 --> 00:10:19,079
It has got to be solved.

187
00:10:19,079 --> 00:10:22,680
It is like going... If one has cancer,

188
00:10:22,680 --> 00:10:25,660
one is serious about it,

189
00:10:25,660 --> 00:10:28,640
you don't play around with it.

190
00:10:28,640 --> 00:10:32,000
Action in relation to the seriousness, then,

191
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:33,599
is instantaneous.

192
00:10:33,599 --> 00:10:35,839
Obviously. Yes.

193
00:10:35,839 --> 00:10:39,920
This raises not an additional question.

194
00:10:39,920 --> 00:10:43,000
I don't mean to go beyond where we haven't begun,

195
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:44,640
in that sense,

196
00:10:44,640 --> 00:10:52,640
but time assumes for the serious person

197
00:10:52,680 --> 00:10:58,640
something very different for his undergoing

198
00:10:58,640 --> 00:11:02,920
than it would seem to be for the unserious person.

199
00:11:02,920 --> 00:11:04,900
One wouldn't have, then, the

200
00:11:04,900 --> 00:11:06,880
feeling of something being dragged out,

201
00:11:06,880 --> 00:11:08,739
or, as we say in English,

202
00:11:08,739 --> 00:11:10,599
time that has to be put in.

203
00:11:10,599 --> 00:11:12,839
Put in, quite.

204
00:11:12,839 --> 00:11:21,560
As a matter of fact, one, in this concurrent communication,

205
00:11:21,560 --> 00:11:22,680
in which communion,

206
00:11:22,680 --> 00:11:27,959
is abidingly present.

207
00:11:27,959 --> 00:11:32,920
Time as such would not in any way oppress.

208
00:11:32,920 --> 00:11:34,439
No, sir. No, sir.

209
00:11:34,439 --> 00:11:35,839
Am I...? Quite right.

210
00:11:35,839 --> 00:11:39,160
But you see, sir,

211
00:11:39,160 --> 00:11:43,379
I am trying to see

212
00:11:43,379 --> 00:11:47,599
what it means to be serious.

213
00:11:47,599 --> 00:11:52,160
The intent,

214
00:11:52,160 --> 00:11:56,160
the urge,

215
00:11:56,160 --> 00:12:03,160
the feeling of total responsibility,

216
00:12:03,160 --> 00:12:08,160
the feeling of action, the doing,

217
00:12:08,160 --> 00:12:11,160
not, I will do.

218
00:12:11,160 --> 00:12:16,160
All that is implied in that word seriousness.

219
00:12:16,160 --> 00:12:21,560
At least I put all those things into that word.

220
00:12:21,560 --> 00:12:22,040
But, sir,

221
00:12:22,040 --> 00:12:25,800
could we look for a moment at one of them

222
00:12:25,800 --> 00:12:30,800
that you put into them, responsibility,

223
00:12:30,800 --> 00:12:35,280
able to be responsive?

224
00:12:35,280 --> 00:12:40,280
That's right. To respond adequately.

225
00:12:40,280 --> 00:12:43,040
Yes, to respond adequately.

226
00:12:43,040 --> 00:12:46,280
To any challenge.

227
00:12:46,280 --> 00:12:48,780
The challenge now is that

228
00:12:48,780 --> 00:12:51,280
the world is in a mess,

229
00:12:51,280 --> 00:12:54,280
confusion, sorrow and every...

230
00:12:54,280 --> 00:12:55,720
violent, all that.

231
00:12:55,720 --> 00:12:58,120
I must, as a human

232
00:12:58,120 --> 00:13:00,520
being who has created this thing,

233
00:13:00,520 --> 00:13:05,520
I must respond adequately.

234
00:13:05,520 --> 00:13:12,800
The adequacy depends on my seriousness in that sense,

235
00:13:12,800 --> 00:13:21,160
on my observation of the chaos,

236
00:13:21,160 --> 00:13:25,160
and responding not according to my prejudices,

237
00:13:25,160 --> 00:13:29,160
my inclination or tendencies, or pleasures or fears,

238
00:13:29,160 --> 00:13:32,160
but responding to the problem,

239
00:13:32,160 --> 00:13:38,160
not according to my translation of the problem.

240
00:13:38,160 --> 00:13:43,160
Yes, I'm just thinking, as you are speaking,

241
00:13:43,160 --> 00:13:50,160
about how difficult it is to...

242
00:13:51,160 --> 00:13:56,160
to communicate this to the person who is thinking

243
00:13:56,160 --> 00:14:03,160
that the way adequately to respond to this chaos

244
00:14:03,160 --> 00:14:06,660
is to have a plan for

245
00:14:06,660 --> 00:14:10,160
it, which one superimposes on it.

246
00:14:10,160 --> 00:14:14,160
And that's exactly what we assume.

247
00:14:14,160 --> 00:14:17,160
And if the plan doesn't work out, we blame ourselves...

248
00:14:17,160 --> 00:14:18,160
Or change the plan.

249
00:14:18,160 --> 00:14:20,160
Or we change the plan, yes.

250
00:14:20,160 --> 00:14:23,160
But we don't respond to the challenge.

251
00:14:23,160 --> 00:14:24,160
No.

252
00:14:24,160 --> 00:14:30,160
We respond according to our conclusion about the problem.

253
00:14:30,160 --> 00:14:32,160
Exactly.

254
00:14:32,160 --> 00:14:35,160
Therefore it means really, sir,

255
00:14:35,160 --> 00:14:38,160
if you can explore it a little more,

256
00:14:38,160 --> 00:14:44,160
the observer is the observed.

257
00:14:44,160 --> 00:14:49,160
Therefore the change, if it comes, is total.

258
00:14:49,160 --> 00:14:50,160
Yes, that's right.

259
00:14:50,160 --> 00:14:51,160
Not partial.

260
00:14:51,160 --> 00:14:54,160
One is no longer outside what he is operating upon.

261
00:14:54,160 --> 00:14:55,160
That's right.

262
00:14:55,160 --> 00:14:59,160
And what he is operating upon is not outside himself.

263
00:14:59,160 --> 00:15:01,160
Because, as we said yesterday,

264
00:15:01,160 --> 00:15:05,160
it's very interesting, if we go into it rather deeply,

265
00:15:05,160 --> 00:15:10,160
the world is me, I am the world.

266
00:15:10,160 --> 00:15:15,160
That's not an intellectual or emotional, but a fact.

267
00:15:15,160 --> 00:15:19,160
Now, when I approach this,

268
00:15:19,160 --> 00:15:24,160
the problem, the chaos, the misery, the suffering,

269
00:15:24,160 --> 00:15:26,160
the violence and all that,

270
00:15:26,160 --> 00:15:30,160
I approach it with my conclusions,

271
00:15:30,160 --> 00:15:34,160
with my fears, with my despairs.

272
00:15:34,160 --> 00:15:38,160
I don't look at the problem.

273
00:15:38,160 --> 00:15:42,160
Well, would you think it

274
00:15:42,160 --> 00:15:46,160
possible to put it this way,

275
00:15:46,160 --> 00:15:49,160
that one doesn't make room for the problem?

276
00:15:49,160 --> 00:15:51,160
Yes, yes, put it in a way...

277
00:15:51,160 --> 00:15:52,160
Would that be all right?

278
00:15:52,160 --> 00:15:53,160
Yes.

279
00:15:53,160 --> 00:15:55,160
One day there is...

280
00:15:55,160 --> 00:16:01,160
Sir, let's look at this.

281
00:16:01,160 --> 00:16:03,160
I have...

282
00:16:03,160 --> 00:16:08,160
As a human being, one has created this misery,

283
00:16:08,160 --> 00:16:12,160
which is called the society in which we live,

284
00:16:12,160 --> 00:16:15,160
an immoral society.

285
00:16:15,160 --> 00:16:16,160
Oh, yes.

286
00:16:16,160 --> 00:16:19,160
Completely immoral.

287
00:16:19,160 --> 00:16:23,160
As a human being, one has created that.

288
00:16:23,160 --> 00:16:27,160
But that human being, looking at it, separates himself

289
00:16:27,160 --> 00:16:33,160
and says, I must do something about it.

290
00:16:33,160 --> 00:16:39,160
The it is me.

291
00:16:39,160 --> 00:16:43,160
Some people respond to that this way.

292
00:16:43,160 --> 00:16:46,160
They say, well, look,

293
00:16:46,160 --> 00:16:49,160
if I...

294
00:16:49,160 --> 00:16:52,160
I'm truly serious, I'm truly responsible,

295
00:16:52,160 --> 00:16:54,160
I make this act,

296
00:16:54,160 --> 00:16:57,160
and there comes between me and the world

297
00:16:57,160 --> 00:17:01,160
this confluent relationship,

298
00:17:01,160 --> 00:17:05,159
which is total.

299
00:17:05,159 --> 00:17:07,659
All the things that are going

300
00:17:07,659 --> 00:17:10,159
on out there that are atrocious,

301
00:17:10,159 --> 00:17:12,159
let's say, 2500 miles away

302
00:17:12,159 --> 00:17:14,159
from where I am, don't stop.

303
00:17:14,159 --> 00:17:16,159
Therefore, how can I stop?

304
00:17:16,160 --> 00:17:20,160
How can I say that the whole world is me

305
00:17:20,160 --> 00:17:22,160
and I am the whole world?

306
00:17:22,160 --> 00:17:26,160
This objection comes up again and again.

307
00:17:26,160 --> 00:17:28,660
I'm interested to know what

308
00:17:28,660 --> 00:17:31,160
your reply to that would be.

309
00:17:31,160 --> 00:17:35,160
Sir, look,

310
00:17:35,160 --> 00:17:40,160
we are human beings irrespective of our labels

311
00:17:40,160 --> 00:17:44,160
– English, French, German, all the rest of it.

312
00:17:44,160 --> 00:17:46,160
Mm-hm.

313
00:17:46,160 --> 00:17:50,160
A human being living in America or in India

314
00:17:50,160 --> 00:17:56,160
has the problems of relationship, of suffering,

315
00:17:56,160 --> 00:18:01,160
of jealousy, envy, greed, ambition, imitation, conformity,

316
00:18:01,160 --> 00:18:03,660
and all that are our

317
00:18:03,660 --> 00:18:06,160
problems, common to both of us.

318
00:18:06,160 --> 00:18:08,160
Yes.

319
00:18:08,160 --> 00:18:10,660
And when I say the

320
00:18:10,660 --> 00:18:13,160
world is me and the world...

321
00:18:13,160 --> 00:18:16,160
me is the world and the world I am,

322
00:18:16,160 --> 00:18:22,160
I see that as a reality, not as a concept.

323
00:18:22,160 --> 00:18:23,160
Mm-hm.

324
00:18:23,160 --> 00:18:31,160
Now, my responsibility to the challenge,

325
00:18:31,160 --> 00:18:33,160
to be adequate,

326
00:18:33,160 --> 00:18:39,160
must be not in terms of what I think,

327
00:18:39,160 --> 00:18:42,160
but what the problem is.

328
00:18:42,160 --> 00:18:44,160
Mm-hm.

329
00:18:44,160 --> 00:18:49,160
Yes, I follow you, I'm sure, here.

330
00:18:49,160 --> 00:18:52,160
I was thinking while you were saying that

331
00:18:52,160 --> 00:18:56,160
that it might have been possible

332
00:18:56,160 --> 00:18:58,160
to answer the question that I posed,

333
00:18:58,160 --> 00:19:02,160
and I'm posing the question simply because

334
00:19:02,160 --> 00:19:05,160
I know some persons who might very well view this

335
00:19:05,160 --> 00:19:08,160
who would raise that and want to participate

336
00:19:08,160 --> 00:19:11,160
with us in this conversation.

337
00:19:11,160 --> 00:19:13,160
I wondered,

338
00:19:14,160 --> 00:19:16,160
whether you might have said that

339
00:19:16,160 --> 00:19:19,160
as soon as one puts it that way,

340
00:19:19,160 --> 00:19:22,160
one has already divorced himself...

341
00:19:22,160 --> 00:19:23,160
That's right.

342
00:19:23,160 --> 00:19:25,160
...from the issue.

343
00:19:25,160 --> 00:19:28,160
That in the practical order,

344
00:19:28,160 --> 00:19:33,160
that question is an interposition

345
00:19:33,160 --> 00:19:37,160
that simply does not have a place

346
00:19:37,160 --> 00:19:40,160
in the activity that you are talking about.

347
00:19:40,160 --> 00:19:42,160
Yes, that's right.

348
00:19:42,160 --> 00:19:43,160
Now, this is very interesting,

349
00:19:43,160 --> 00:19:46,660
because it means that the

350
00:19:46,660 --> 00:19:50,160
person must suspend his disbelief...

351
00:19:50,160 --> 00:19:51,160
Or his belief.

352
00:19:51,160 --> 00:19:52,160
Or his belief.

353
00:19:52,160 --> 00:19:54,160
Yes.

354
00:19:54,160 --> 00:19:55,160
And observe the thing.

355
00:19:55,160 --> 00:19:57,160
And observe the thing.

356
00:19:57,160 --> 00:19:59,160
Which is not possible

357
00:19:59,160 --> 00:20:05,160
if the observer is different from the observed.

358
00:20:05,160 --> 00:20:13,160
Now, would you explore the practical aspect

359
00:20:13,160 --> 00:20:21,160
of this with me for a moment?

360
00:20:21,160 --> 00:20:24,160
People will say,

361
00:20:24,160 --> 00:20:27,160
who up to this point are listening,

362
00:20:27,160 --> 00:20:33,160
it would seem,

363
00:20:33,160 --> 00:20:36,160
people at this point will say,

364
00:20:36,160 --> 00:20:40,160
well, yes, but I can't stop it.

365
00:20:40,160 --> 00:20:43,160
I think I have...

366
00:20:43,160 --> 00:20:47,160
I have an intuition of what you mean, they'll say.

367
00:20:47,160 --> 00:20:52,160
But the minute that I open myself,

368
00:20:52,160 --> 00:20:55,160
or begin to open myself,

369
00:20:55,160 --> 00:21:00,160
all these things seem to rush in on me.

370
00:21:00,160 --> 00:21:05,160
What I had hoped doesn't seem to take place.

371
00:21:05,160 --> 00:21:08,160
If I understand you correctly,

372
00:21:08,160 --> 00:21:10,160
they are really not doing what they claim

373
00:21:10,160 --> 00:21:12,160
that they are trying to do.

374
00:21:12,160 --> 00:21:13,160
That's right.

375
00:21:13,160 --> 00:21:20,160
Sir, can we put this question differently?

376
00:21:20,160 --> 00:21:26,160
What is a human being to do,

377
00:21:26,160 --> 00:21:32,160
confronted with this problem of suffering, chaos,

378
00:21:32,160 --> 00:21:34,160
all that is going on round us?

379
00:21:34,160 --> 00:21:35,160
Yes.

380
00:21:35,160 --> 00:21:40,160
What is he to do?

381
00:21:40,160 --> 00:21:43,160
He approaches it generally

382
00:21:43,160 --> 00:21:48,160
with a conclusion,

383
00:21:48,160 --> 00:21:52,160
what he should do about it.

384
00:21:52,160 --> 00:21:55,160
And this conclusion is interposed between him...

385
00:21:55,160 --> 00:22:01,160
Yes, the conclusion is the factor of separation.

386
00:22:01,160 --> 00:22:03,160
Right.

387
00:22:03,160 --> 00:22:10,160
Now, can he observe the fact of this confusion

388
00:22:10,160 --> 00:22:13,160
without any conclusions?

389
00:22:13,160 --> 00:22:17,160
Without any planning,

390
00:22:17,160 --> 00:22:23,160
without any predetermined way

391
00:22:23,160 --> 00:22:27,160
of getting out of this chaos?

392
00:22:27,160 --> 00:22:34,160
Because his predetermined conclusions,

393
00:22:34,160 --> 00:22:36,160
ideas and so on,

394
00:22:36,160 --> 00:22:42,160
are all derived from the past.

395
00:22:42,160 --> 00:22:49,160
And the past is trying to resolve the problem.

396
00:22:49,160 --> 00:22:51,160
Yes, yes.

397
00:22:51,160 --> 00:22:54,160
And therefore he is translating it

398
00:22:54,160 --> 00:22:58,160
and acting according to his previous conclusions,

399
00:22:58,160 --> 00:23:03,160
whereas the fact demands that you look at it.

400
00:23:03,160 --> 00:23:05,160
The fact demands that you observe it,

401
00:23:05,160 --> 00:23:08,160
that you listen to it.

402
00:23:08,160 --> 00:23:11,160
The fact itself will have the answer,

403
00:23:11,160 --> 00:23:15,160
you don't have to bring the answer to it.

404
00:23:15,160 --> 00:23:17,160
I wonder if I am making myself clear.

405
00:23:17,160 --> 00:23:20,160
Yes, I am listening very, very hard.

406
00:23:20,160 --> 00:23:23,160
I really am.

407
00:23:23,160 --> 00:23:29,160
I am afraid if I am not going beyond

408
00:23:29,160 --> 00:23:34,160
where I shouldn't, haven't yet begun,

409
00:23:34,160 --> 00:23:41,160
the next question that would naturally arise here

410
00:23:41,160 --> 00:23:45,160
or perhaps you might feel when I raise the question

411
00:23:45,160 --> 00:23:47,160
that it is the wrong question.

412
00:23:47,160 --> 00:23:54,160
But can one communicate

413
00:23:54,160 --> 00:24:01,160
in the sense that we have been unravelling this?

414
00:24:01,160 --> 00:24:06,160
One says, I don't know.

415
00:24:06,160 --> 00:24:09,160
It doesn't seem to me that I have done this.

416
00:24:09,160 --> 00:24:11,160
One says, I haven't done this yet.

417
00:24:11,160 --> 00:24:15,160
I can recognise all the things

418
00:24:15,160 --> 00:24:18,160
that have been described that are terrible.

419
00:24:18,160 --> 00:24:21,160
I don't recognise all the things

420
00:24:21,160 --> 00:24:25,160
that appear to be promised

421
00:24:25,160 --> 00:24:28,160
without suggesting that I am imagining them

422
00:24:28,160 --> 00:24:30,160
or projecting them out there.

423
00:24:30,160 --> 00:24:31,160
Clearly, if there is to be a change,

424
00:24:31,160 --> 00:24:33,160
it has to be a change that is altogether radical.

425
00:24:33,160 --> 00:24:34,160
Yes.

426
00:24:34,160 --> 00:24:37,160
Now, I must start. What do I do?

427
00:24:37,160 --> 00:24:40,160
Sir, there are two things involved, aren't there?

428
00:24:40,160 --> 00:24:41,160
Yes.

429
00:24:41,160 --> 00:24:51,160
First, I must learn from the problem,

430
00:24:51,160 --> 00:24:54,160
which means I must have a mind

431
00:24:54,160 --> 00:25:00,160
that has a quality of humility.

432
00:25:00,160 --> 00:25:02,660
It doesn't come to a

433
00:25:02,660 --> 00:25:05,160
sense, I know all about it.

434
00:25:05,160 --> 00:25:09,160
What he knows is merely explanations,

435
00:25:09,160 --> 00:25:11,160
rational or irrational.

436
00:25:12,160 --> 00:25:16,660
He comes to the problem

437
00:25:16,660 --> 00:25:21,160
with rational or irrational solutions.

438
00:25:21,160 --> 00:25:26,160
Therefore he is not learning from the problem.

439
00:25:28,160 --> 00:25:32,160
The problem will reveal an infinite lot of things

440
00:25:32,160 --> 00:25:34,160
if I am capable of looking

441
00:25:34,160 --> 00:25:36,160
at it and learning about it.

442
00:25:36,160 --> 00:25:39,160
And for that I must have a sense of humility.

443
00:25:39,160 --> 00:25:41,160
I am saying, I don't know.

444
00:25:41,160 --> 00:25:45,160
This is a tremendous problem, let me look at it,

445
00:25:45,160 --> 00:25:47,160
let me learn about it,

446
00:25:47,160 --> 00:25:52,160
not I come to it with my conclusions.

447
00:25:52,160 --> 00:25:56,160
Therefore I will stop learning about the problem.

448
00:25:57,160 --> 00:26:02,160
Are you suggesting that this act

449
00:26:02,160 --> 00:26:06,160
is a waiting on the problem to reveal itself?

450
00:26:06,160 --> 00:26:08,160
That's right.

451
00:26:08,160 --> 00:26:15,160
Therefore I must be capable of looking at it.

452
00:26:15,160 --> 00:26:17,160
I cannot look at it if

453
00:26:17,160 --> 00:26:19,160
I come to it with ideas,

454
00:26:19,160 --> 00:26:21,160
with ideations, with mentations,

455
00:26:21,160 --> 00:26:24,160
of all very kind and conclusions.

456
00:26:24,160 --> 00:26:26,160
I must come to it

457
00:26:26,160 --> 00:26:28,160
and say, look, what is it?

458
00:26:28,160 --> 00:26:32,160
Not learn, I must learn from it,

459
00:26:32,160 --> 00:26:35,160
not learn according to some professor,

460
00:26:35,160 --> 00:26:37,160
some psychologist, some philosopher.

461
00:26:37,160 --> 00:26:50,160
That one has the capacity for this.

462
00:26:50,160 --> 00:26:52,160
Some persons would suggest.

463
00:26:52,160 --> 00:26:55,160
I don't give a... Sir, we are so vain.

464
00:26:55,160 --> 00:27:00,160
But this doesn't mean anything for the doing

465
00:27:00,160 --> 00:27:03,160
of what must be done, that there is a capacity.

466
00:27:03,160 --> 00:27:06,160
No. The learning is the doing.

467
00:27:06,160 --> 00:27:09,160
Exactly. Yes, yes.

468
00:27:09,160 --> 00:27:12,160
I wanted to make that clear because we comfort ourselves

469
00:27:12,160 --> 00:27:15,160
with the curious notion, if I've been following you,

470
00:27:15,160 --> 00:27:21,160
that we possess a possibility,

471
00:27:21,160 --> 00:27:25,160
and because we possess the possibility

472
00:27:25,160 --> 00:27:29,160
we think that some day it will actualise itself, perhaps.

473
00:27:29,160 --> 00:27:31,160
Quite, quite.

474
00:27:31,160 --> 00:27:35,160
But if I'm correct both ways,

475
00:27:35,160 --> 00:27:40,160
no possibility can actualise itself,

476
00:27:40,160 --> 00:27:44,160
and in the practical order that never occurs.

477
00:27:44,160 --> 00:27:47,160
But somehow it's believed, isn't it?

478
00:27:47,160 --> 00:27:50,160
I'm afraid it is. It is believed.

479
00:27:50,160 --> 00:27:55,160
Sir, it is really quite simple.

480
00:27:55,160 --> 00:28:00,160
There is this misery, confusion,

481
00:28:00,160 --> 00:28:05,160
immense sorrow in the world, violence, all that.

482
00:28:05,160 --> 00:28:11,160
I have... human beings have created it.

483
00:28:11,160 --> 00:28:17,160
Human beings have built a structure of society

484
00:28:17,160 --> 00:28:22,160
which sustains this chaos.

485
00:28:22,160 --> 00:28:24,160
That's a fact.

486
00:28:24,160 --> 00:28:25,660
Now, I come to it,

487
00:28:25,660 --> 00:28:27,160
a human being comes to it,

488
00:28:27,160 --> 00:28:32,160
trying to resolve it according to his plan,

489
00:28:32,160 --> 00:28:34,160
according to his prejudices,

490
00:28:34,160 --> 00:28:35,160
his instincts,

491
00:28:35,160 --> 00:28:39,160
his idiosyncrasies or knowledge.

492
00:28:39,160 --> 00:28:40,160
Why?

493
00:28:40,160 --> 00:28:47,160
Which means he has already understood the problem.

494
00:28:48,160 --> 00:28:53,160
Whereas the problem is always new.

495
00:28:53,160 --> 00:28:59,160
So I must come to it afresh.

496
00:29:00,160 --> 00:29:04,160
One of the things that has concerned me

497
00:29:04,160 --> 00:29:09,160
for many, many years as a reader,

498
00:29:09,160 --> 00:29:11,160
as a student,

499
00:29:11,160 --> 00:29:18,160
as one whose daily work

500
00:29:18,160 --> 00:29:21,160
involves the study of scriptures,

501
00:29:21,160 --> 00:29:27,160
is the recurrent statement

502
00:29:27,160 --> 00:29:29,160
that one comes upon,

503
00:29:29,160 --> 00:29:33,160
sometimes in a very dramatic form.

504
00:29:33,160 --> 00:29:37,160
Take the prophetic ministry of Jesus,

505
00:29:37,160 --> 00:29:44,160
where he speaks,

506
00:29:44,160 --> 00:29:48,160
and he says that they are hearing,

507
00:29:48,160 --> 00:29:52,160
but they are not listening.

508
00:29:52,160 --> 00:29:54,160
They are observing,

509
00:29:54,160 --> 00:29:56,160
but they are not seeing.

510
00:29:56,160 --> 00:29:57,160
And doing.

511
00:29:57,160 --> 00:30:02,160
But then...

512
00:30:02,160 --> 00:30:07,160
it seems...

513
00:30:07,160 --> 00:30:10,160
that he doesn't say,

514
00:30:10,160 --> 00:30:13,160
in order to attain to that,

515
00:30:13,160 --> 00:30:14,160
do this.

516
00:30:14,160 --> 00:30:17,160
No, the closest he comes to it

517
00:30:17,160 --> 00:30:21,160
is through the analogy with the child,

518
00:30:21,160 --> 00:30:24,160
to have faith as a little child.

519
00:30:24,160 --> 00:30:27,160
Now, I don't want to talk about words here,

520
00:30:27,160 --> 00:30:29,160
because that would be disastrous.

521
00:30:29,160 --> 00:30:31,160
So what's meant by faith here?

522
00:30:31,160 --> 00:30:33,160
What's meant by faith here is not something

523
00:30:33,160 --> 00:30:35,160
that perhaps we would probably go into.

524
00:30:35,160 --> 00:30:37,160
But the analogy with the child

525
00:30:37,160 --> 00:30:40,160
suggests that the child is doing something

526
00:30:40,160 --> 00:30:43,160
that is lost somewhere along the way,

527
00:30:43,160 --> 00:30:44,160
in some respect.

528
00:30:44,160 --> 00:30:47,160
I'm sure he didn't mean that there's a perfect continuity

529
00:30:47,160 --> 00:30:49,160
between the adult and the child.

530
00:30:49,160 --> 00:30:50,160
But there's...

531
00:30:50,160 --> 00:30:52,160
Why is it, over the centuries,

532
00:30:52,160 --> 00:30:56,160
that men have said this over and over again,

533
00:30:56,160 --> 00:30:59,160
namely, you're not listening,

534
00:30:59,160 --> 00:31:01,160
you're not seeing,

535
00:31:01,160 --> 00:31:06,160
and then they don't point to an operation,

536
00:31:06,160 --> 00:31:09,160
they point to an analogy,

537
00:31:09,160 --> 00:31:10,160
and then some of them

538
00:31:10,160 --> 00:31:11,160
don't even point to an analogy,

539
00:31:11,160 --> 00:31:13,160
they just hold up a flower.

540
00:31:13,160 --> 00:31:19,160
Sir, look, we live on words.

541
00:31:19,160 --> 00:31:21,160
Most people live on words.

542
00:31:21,160 --> 00:31:25,160
They don't go beyond the word.

543
00:31:25,160 --> 00:31:29,160
And what we are talking about

544
00:31:29,160 --> 00:31:31,160
is not only the word,

545
00:31:31,160 --> 00:31:33,160
the meaning of the word,

546
00:31:33,160 --> 00:31:36,160
the communication that exists in using words,

547
00:31:36,160 --> 00:31:40,160
but the non-verbal communication

548
00:31:40,160 --> 00:31:44,160
which is having an insight.

549
00:31:44,160 --> 00:31:45,660
That's what we are talking

550
00:31:45,660 --> 00:31:47,160
about all the time, so far.

551
00:31:47,160 --> 00:31:48,160
Yes.

552
00:31:48,160 --> 00:31:53,160
That is, the mind can only have an insight

553
00:31:53,160 --> 00:31:59,160
if it is capable of listening.

554
00:31:59,160 --> 00:32:01,160
And you may say,

555
00:32:01,160 --> 00:32:04,660
you do listen when the

556
00:32:04,660 --> 00:32:08,160
crisis is right at your doorstep.

557
